From 75a14e05f15f620cbc5370661ef7e7021713fb50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BANCO audit <waelzaid66@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:47:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] proof: P0-4 the web seller workspace can create a listing
 again

For verification only, on the audit proof branch.

Measured: with every rendered field filled, the API rejected all three
categories. The form renders no field for condition (car), offer_type or
rental_term (real estate) or capacity (industrial), and buildSpecsObject
iterates only over rendered fields, so no value for those keys could ever
be sent. 0 of 3 categories were creatable, in every context.

The required-attribute contract lived in three places kept in step by a
comment in validateAttributes. It is now one shared module,
@workspace/taxonomy/listings: requiredSpecKeys mirrors the server floor,
and the web form derives both its field list and its required marks from
it. The real-estate rules are context-aware in both directions, as the
API is: rent adds rental_term, land and bare commercial units drop rooms
and finishing.

Two executable controls replace the comment, each proven to fail without
the fix:
  api-server ListingService.requiredSpecKeys.test.ts compares the shared
  contract to validateAttributes by mutation - fill, drop one key, see
  whether the verdict flips.
  banco-web/banco-website tests/workspace-listing-form.test.mjs asserts
  every gating key has a field a seller can fill, in all six contexts.
  13 of its 32 assertions fail on the pre-fix form.

The static parity audit passed throughout, because substring checks
cannot see a payload. It audited 18 paths on banco-web and none on
banco-website, which ships the same workspace from byte-identical files.
It now runs every check on both surfaces, compares the twin files by
hash, and declares its own size: 18 checks to 40.

API suite 518 passed / 3 skipped / 0 failed via the official runner on a
database created for the run. banco-web and banco-website 32/32 each.
Chain gate 245/245, confidence 24/24, parity 40/40. Every project
typechecks clean; api-server still carries the 11 known P0-5 listingId
errors and no others.
